<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico to drain 4.300 bln pesos.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico to drain 4.300 bln pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico sought to drain 4.300 billion pesos from the secondary market on Wednesday through a combination of three direct sales of paper and seven repurchase agreements, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were offered or assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    351 days   22.13 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    176 days</p>
<p>    150 million     85 days</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    400 million     47 days</p>
<p>    500 million     42 days</p>
<p>    700 million     34 days</p>
<p>    600 million     33 days</p>
<p>    500 million     12 days</p>
<p>    450 million	5 days</p>
<p>    700 million	1 days</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
